//! # Responsibility
//!
//! This module is responsible for the Markdown help manual as a whole: rendering
//! one page per registered leaf command plus the index, deciding the write
//! order, and driving the write so a failure never mixes Clio's generated files
//! with a directory's other content.
//!
//! ## Owns
//! - `write_manual`, the validate-all-then-write entry point the help dispatch
//!   calls
//! - The manual's render: one page per registered leaf command, sorted, plus
//!   the index page
//! - The generated-by marker that decides which files this command may replace
//! - The incomplete-manual error shape a failed write step reports
//!
//! ## Does not own
//! - The held output directory and the per-page operations inside it: the
//!   component walk, the target check, the temp write, and the promote (see
//!   `cli_manual_write_dir`)
//! - A single page's Markdown (see `cli_help_markdown`)
//! - The registry records rendered (see `cli_command_registry`)
//! - The `--markdown`/`--out` argument validation (see `cli_top_level`)
//! - The CLI error shape and exit codes (see `cli_error`)
//!
//! ## Boundary
//!
//! Changes to which files the manual writes and in what order should normally
//! require changes here. Changes to how one page reaches the output directory
//! should not.
//!
//! Keep this module focused on the manual's content and write order.

use crate::cli_command_registry;
use crate::cli_command_spec::CommandSpec;
use crate::cli_error::CliError;
use crate::cli_help_markdown::{PageMap, render_command_page};
use crate::cli_manual_write_dir::OutDir;
use std::path::Path;

#[cfg(test)]
